-- title:
--   Admissible small-constant field k₀ for the descended Igusa base
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a level $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Assume given: a finset $W$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ (rational affine geometric places at which the generating $j$-invariant takes a supersingular value); an inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` in `fieldBar q M'`; a `ConstantReduction` datum $R_0$ over $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is, a valuation subring of integers together with a surjective residue map with kernel its maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and a degree- and order-preserving map on places, subject to `hR₀`: every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is an integer of $R_0$ with residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; an index $\zeta$ in `Idx q`; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction, each $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to $\ell$ under `redQ`, $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective, and the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ permute the family; $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets the constants exactly in $A$, is fixed by all `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, contains a coordinate $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$, and receives the integers $f$ of $R_0$ that are regular wherever $\hat\jmath=$ `coeffEmb jq` is and whose residue is an integer at $s$, with $f-a$ in the maximal ideal whenever the residue of $a\in A$ equals the value of the residue of $f$ at $s$. Assume further a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi\in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $\iota\colon A_0\to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A\cap K_0$, inducing a surjection onto $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, and a uniformiser $\varpi_0$ of $A_0$ with $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$; and the subfield $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, which contains $\hat\jmath$, together with an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ whose structure map is induced by $\iota$. The conclusion: there are an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $k_0$ and $K_0$ have the same underlying set and $\pi_0=\pi$, and moreover $A\cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0\cap A$, there is a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ and a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $k_0$, there is a unit $u$ of $A$ with $\pi_0^{q^2-1}=qu$, and there is a ring isomorphism $A_0\cong A\cap k_0$ compatible with $\iota$ under the inclusion of $k_0$.
--
--   This records, in one statement, that the descent field $K_0$ — realised as an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ — is an admissible field of small constants for the base of the descended Igusa/Drinfeld two-chart model: a henselian discrete valuation ring with tame uniformiser $\pi_0$, algebraically closed residue field exhausting the residues of $A$, the requisite roots of unity, and a transport isomorphism $A_0\cong A\cap k_0$. It is used by the subsequent statements about the bottom layer and level field of this model and about formal smoothness of the Igusa subalgebra in the descent.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_admissible_smallConstants_of_descentBase.lean

